# 25. Final Mental Model

Imagine several isolated villages.

Every possible road has a construction cost.

The goal is to connect all villages while avoiding unnecessary roads.

Therefore:

> Repeatedly choose the cheapest safe road that connects currently separated parts of the graph.

## Kruskal

```text
Choose the cheapest roads globally.
Use DSU to connect separate components.
```

## Prim

```text
Start from one village.
Use a min-heap to grow one connected network.
```

## Most Important Intuition

```text
MST is not just about choosing cheap edges.

MST is about choosing cheap edges that safely connect
currently separated parts of the graph.
```
